            <div xml:id="d542">

                <pb facs="0787" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg671"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Lincheng/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-29T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1923—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 29—7:53
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>242. Your 121, June 23, 3 p.m., last sentence. My 234, June 22, 10 a.m. Major
                    Allen has increased demand for indemnity in behalf of self, wife and son to
                    $150,000 gold.</p>
                <p>Holcomb, formerly United States district attorney, Shanghai, who is acting as
                    counsel for four other American victims of Lincheng outrage now in Shanghai has
                    come to Peking to consult Legation regarding their claims and informs me his
                    clients intend to demand $150,000 gold each as exemplary damages.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
